                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "The present dataset presents the Conclusions of the European Committee of Social Rights of the Council of Europe in the context of the \r\nreporting system of the European Social Charter on the issue of tobacco control. \r\n\r\nTo our knowledge, this is the first mapping on the matter and \r\nit aspires to demonstrate the extent to which tobacco control connects to the implementation of human rights’ obligations and in particular to \r\nthe monitoring of the rights enshrined in the European Social Charter.\r\n\r\nThe dataset has been developed as part the study into novel smoke-free policies carried out at the Global Health Law Groningen Research \r\nCentre of the University of Groningen and is financed by the Dutch Heart Foundation, the Lung Foundation Netherlands, the Dutch Cancer\r\nSociety, the Dutch Diabetes Research Foundation & the Netherlands Thrombosis Foundation.\r\n\r\nMethods include systematic searches of the ECSR’ Conclusions that are publicly available on HUDOC-ESC until December 2020.\r\n\r\nThe relevant sources are hyperlinked. Search terms used include *tobacco, *smoking, *cigarette, *smoke (excl *black smoke, *industrial smoke \r\netc).\r\n\r\nThe funders have not been involved in any of the study design, data collection and analysis."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
